>meantime, if you switch your monitor to black and white/2 colors, the
>problem will not occur.  I do this using the Switcheroo FKEY right before
>the list is displayed.

Hmmm... I think I'd find it annoying to convert to black and white
every time I died.  If you have compiled nethack yourself, you may
want to modify it so that it doesn't use alert boxes at all.  The
refresh problem occurs because an update event gets posted after the
alert goes away.  Your inventory is printed, and then nethack takes
care of the update event by redrawing the screen (incorrectly).
Fixing this would require that the mac window updating routine know
about the pager, and whether it was in full screen mode or not.

In either case, I find the screen updating too slow in the first
place, so I prefer getting rid of the alerts anyway.  Look for
occurances of the two routines which handle alerts (I forget the
names, but something like MacUseAlert() or something) and change the
#ifdef MACOS in front of it to something mnemonic like #ifdef MAC_USE_ALERTS.

In either case, thanks to the development team (both mac and general)
for an outstanding game.

